Compiling and Linking an Assembly Program in NASM
•	Type the above code using a text editor and save it as hello.nasm. 
•	Make sure that you are in the same directory as where you saved hello.nasm. 
•	To assemble the program, type nasm -f elf64 hello.nasm 
•	If there is any error, you will be prompted about that at this stage. Otherwise an object file of your program named hello.o will be     created. 
•	To link the object file and create an executable file named hello, 
  type ld -o hello hello.o 
•	Execute the program by typing ./hello 
